        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: consolidate exact keyed async queues",
        "body": "Closes #99683\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw carried repeated per-key promise-tail serializers across core and bundled plugins. Each copy independently implemented FIFO ordering, rejection recovery, unrelated-key parallelism, and final-tail cleanup, creating drift risk around the same concurrency invariant.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis migrates 23 exact-contract callers to the existing `enqueueKeyedTask` primitive in `openclaw/plugin-sdk/keyed-async-queue`. Caller-owned tail maps remain where drain, reset, or test behavior observes them.\n\nTimeout eviction, close cancellation, debounce replacement, single-flight caching, and hybrid owner scheduling remain local; the shared helper gains no new options or policy.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. Maintainers and plugin developers now have one tested implementation for exact per-key FIFO serialization, with 244 fewer production lines across the migrated slice.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --maxWorkers=8 <14 explicit files>`: 438 tests passed across 13 shards.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --maxWorkers=8 <8 explicit files>`: 246 tests passed across 7 shards.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/imessage/src/monitor/catchup.test.ts`: 26 tests passed after the type correction.\n- Blacksmith Testbox-through-Crabbox `tbx_01kwn3c71shq3s8nsbd4wkvn71`: `check:changed` passed core/extension typechecks, core/extension lint, repository guards, and runtime import-cycle checks. Actions run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28686960340\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --prompt-file /tmp/keyed-queue-review-notes.md --stream-engine-output`: clean, no accepted/actionable findings, confidence 0.97.\n- `git diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD`: 114 additions, 358 deletions, net `-244` lines across 23 production files.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`: passed.\n",
